# Realtime & Event Systems — Aquarius DeFi Lab

## Core Philosophy
- Realtime exists to surface what is normally unseen.
- Events should be meaningful, not noisy.

## Event Design
- Events must represent real protocol state changes.
- Prefer semantic events over raw logs.
- Every event should answer: "Why does this matter to the user?"

## Streams & Subscriptions
- Design streams to be composable and filterable.
- Avoid protocol-specific coupling in stream interfaces.

## Performance & Reliability
- Assume high-frequency data.
- Backpressure and rate control are mandatory.
- Prefer eventual consistency over dropped events.

## User Experience
- Realtime insights must reduce cognitive load.
- Do not overwhelm users with raw data.
- Aggregate when possible; alert when necessary.

## Summary (Non-Negotiable)
- Aquarius favors event streams over request-response when possible.
- Use WebSockets or SSE for real-time data delivery.
- Do NOT simulate real-time with polling unless explicitly instructed.
- Streams must be protocol-aware (e.g., ethereum, solana).
- Events must be typed and documented.
- Never couple stream logic to UI rendering.
